  "description": "SummitX: dual-motor utility for hills, errands and longer rides. Choose a removable 32Ah or 60Ah battery and switch between front, rear and dual-motor drive to suit your route.\n\nMotor configuration: Front motor: 500W sustained / 1,000W peak. Rear motor: 750W sustained / 1,300W peak. Combined peak output is 2,300W; peak output is not continuous power.\n\nBattery choice: 48V 32Ah (1,536Wh) with a 5A charger, or 48V 60Ah (2,880Wh) with an 8A charger. The 60Ah battery stores 87.5% more energy. Published pedal-assist maximums are up to 100 miles for 32Ah and 160 miles for 60Ah. Actual range varies with speed, hills, cargo, temperature and motor use.\n\nBraking and suspension: Front and rear hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm rotors, a 65mm suspension fork with adjustment and lockout, 20 × 4.0 in tires, and Shimano 7-speed gearing. No rear suspension.\n\nFit and storage: Recommended rider height is 5'4\"–6'4\". Seat height is 35–43.3 in. Folded dimensions are 38.1 × 22 × 35.4 in. Check your fit, storage space and lifting needs before ordering.\n\nVerified bike weights: Without battery: 98.8 lb. With 32Ah: 121.5 lb. With 60Ah: 132.7 lb. Folding reduces storage space, not the weight you need to lift.\n\nEveryday utility: Color LCD, USB Type-C phone charging, integrated headlight and rear brake light. Published total payload is 350 lb including rider and cargo. The rear rack supports up to 110 lb within the total payload limit.\n\nIncluded equipment: Selected battery and charger, battery key, rear rack, fenders, toolkit and user manual. Assembly is required. Current promotional gifts and any separate shipping are shown in the purchase area and cart.\n\nLimited warranty and returns: Frame and front fork: 2 years. Core electrical components: 1 year. Battery: 1 year or 300 charging cycles, whichever comes first. Review the warranty coverage and exclusions and return policy before purchasing. Commercial use, including food delivery, is excluded by the current limited warranty.",
